    {
      "name": "WRAP",
      "type": "built-in",
      "description": "Pause the session without promoting anything. Writes the session summary to sessions.jsonl and overwrites last_session.json so the next boot has continuity — that's it. Does not touch task memory, does not run the verify/accept gate, does not write to semantic memory, does not rotate decisions.jsonl. Use this for 'taking a break' / 'stopping for now' — use MEMORY_CONSOLIDATE or TASK_CLOSE when the work is actually confirmed and ready to promote.",
      "usage": "> OS_COMMAND WRAP"
    },
    {
      "name": "MEMORY_CONSOLIDATE",
      "type": "built-in",
      "description": "Deliberate promotion pass — invoke this when the work is actually confirmed and ready, not just when you're pausing (see WRAP for that). Extract rules from decisions/episodic logs to semantic memory (verify-before-promote, diff-before-delete, dedup — see core.memory.sk), then archive processed decisions.jsonl entries to decisions.archive.jsonl and sweep tasks/ for orphaned files whose branch no longer exists. On a feature/ticket branch, excludes the active task file entirely (untouched until TASK_CLOSE). On a protected branch (main/master/develop/release), the task file there is rolling working memory, not a ticket file — apply the same verify/accept gate as TASK_CLOSE to its contents, promote what qualifies, then clear it (don't archive it as if a ticket finished). Also writes the session summary to sessions.jsonl and overwrites last_session.json.",
      "usage": "> OS_COMMAND MEMORY_CONSOLIDATE"
    },
    {
      "name": "TASK_CLOSE",
      "type": "built-in",
      "description": "Full procedure in core.memory.sk. Resolves the task file for [branch] (default: current branch, sanitized per BOOT.md §2), verifies claims before promoting them to semantic memory, dedups against existing knowledge entries, then physically MOVEs the task file from .ai-os/memory/tasks/ to .ai-os/memory/archived_tasks/. Also writes the session summary to sessions.jsonl and last_session.json.",
      "usage": "> OS_COMMAND TASK_CLOSE [branch]"
    }
  ],
